-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 147  Hyjal round-20 -- the spell wave MoltenFront/13_'s new templates brought
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Expected follow-on, not a regression. MoltenFront/13_ cloned 14 base-phase
-- creature templates and imported their SmartAI with them; those rows reference
-- Cata spells that resolve in NEITHER the built client Spell.dbc NOR
-- acore_world.spell_dbc, so SmartAIMgr skipped them at load. This is precisely
-- the pattern rounds 15-17 documented: every template import surfaces a fresh
-- set of spell references. The post-apply boot log named nine:
--
--   101174  3652135 Malfurion Stormrage        event 0 action 85 (INVOKER_CAST)
--   97605   3652300 Seething Pyrelord          event 0 action 33
--   96693   3652300 Seething Pyrelord          event 2 action 11
--   101195  3652300 Seething Pyrelord          event 4 action 11
--   79878   3652500 Hyjal Defender             event 1 action 11
--   97306   3652633 Lava Burster + 3653112     shared
--   97670   3652834 Wounded Hyjal Defender     event 0 action 80
--   83476   3653107 Smothervine                event 1 action 11
--   98268   3653112 Subterranean Magma Worm    event 4 action 11
--
-- Eight are straight downports from the real Cata 4.3.4 client (Spell.dbc +
-- SpellEffect.dbc out of wow-update-base-15601.MPQ): Fury of the Wolf, Chain
-- Fireball, Seething Rage, Bloodthirst, Lava Spit, Enchanted Salve, Taunt and
-- Burning Hunger.
--
-- 101174 is an EFFECT-ONLY ORPHAN: Blizzard dropped its Spell.dbc row in 4.3.4
-- but kept the SpellEffect row. Verified rather than assumed -- its effect row
-- (effIdx 0, effect 3 = DUMMY, aura 0, base 0, misc 0) is byte-for-byte the same
-- shape as 101173 / 101177 / 101179 / 101182, the four "Molten Front invoker
-- dummy" siblings round 15 already shipped, so it is synthesised with the
-- IDENTICAL tuple those four use and the family stays consistent.
--
-- Two side effects of this file, both good: the boot warnings "Creature entry
-- (3652135) / (3675180) has SmartAI enabled but no SmartAI entries" disappear
-- too -- those creatures HAVE rows, but every one of them was being thrown away
-- because of these missing spells, leaving the creature with nothing valid.
--
-- Generated by HyjalCata/tools/gen_hyjal_spell_downport_r20.py. Matching CLIENT
-- rows are appended to Custom/CSV DBC/Spell.csv and Spell.dbc is recompiled and
-- packed into BOTH patch-4.MPQ and enGB/patch-enGB-3.MPQ.
--
-- Idempotent. Needs a worldserver restart.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (97605,96693,101195,79878,97306,97670,83476,98268,101174);

